  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First release. Sagant is a durable, step-orchestrated workflow engine for .NET: extend , mark methods //, and get retries with compensation, pause/resume, step/workflow timeouts, child workflows, and crash-safe recovery without hand-rolling a state machine.\n\n**Packages**\n-  — runtime-agnostic core: , effects, settings, attributes.\n-  — the reference runtime, backed by a persistent Akka.NET  entity actor per workflow instance.\n-  —  for exercising a workflow's own logic with no , no persistence.\n-  /  — recurring cron/interval schedules that start other workflows on a cadence.\n\n**Highlights**\n- Retries with backoff, failover, and parking a run for a person to resume.\n- Pause-for-approval and operator suspend/resume, both with optional timeouts.\n- Child workflows: fan-out,  groups, completion/failure/remaining-children policies, .\n- At-least-once command delivery via , with an opt-in caller-supplied idempotency key.\n- Full  tracing (one trace per run, correlated across retries/crashes/relocation) and OpenTelemetry metrics.\n-  — a full worked example: multi-step saga, compensation cascades, pause-for-approval, a 3-node Aspire cluster with a live UI.\n\nSee [](https://github.com/yanpitangui/sagant/tree/main/docs) for the full guarantees contract, workflow model, and integration guide.",
